		<boolean name="eventTarget">
			<displayName>Event Target</displayName>
			<description>Nothing reads this. It is what every setDisabled and setInvisible event action disables and hides, according to its condition, in the handlers on the four attribute tabs: focus, blur and change of the text field; picked, cleared, edited and added of the lookup; added, edited, removed, selected and deleted of the grids; and change of the geometry map and list membership. It is a checkbox because only a boolean attribute can be their target. PrimeFaces does not apply these conditions, so only SmartClient changes it.</description>
		</boolean>
